{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00153",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.51,
      "end_seconds": 2.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Right, hello there. Please, sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.89,
      "end_seconds": 4.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.81,
      "end_seconds": 8.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Go ahead, tell me what's happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.53,
      "end_seconds": 18.29,
      "duration_seconds": 9.76,
      "text": "Mainly heartburn. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one. I took the morning off to come in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.19,
      "end_seconds": 21.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.39,
      "end_seconds": 31.5,
      "duration_seconds": 9.11,
      "text": "Probably two days. Yeah. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.84,
      "end_seconds": 40.94,
      "duration_seconds": 9.1,
      "text": "Go on. Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.14,
      "end_seconds": 52.66,
      "duration_seconds": 10.52,
      "text": "It's all the time. Only antacids, and it's not much. Oh, and a cough at night. That's been about the same, two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.08,
      "end_seconds": 55.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Mm-hm. Any vomiting blood or trouble swallowing at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.9,
      "end_seconds": 59.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.44,
      "end_seconds": 63.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "So, any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.73,
      "end_seconds": 67.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.48,
      "end_seconds": 73.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.15,
      "end_seconds": 76.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.89,
      "end_seconds": 81.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.23,
      "end_seconds": 95.65,
      "duration_seconds": 12.42,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.77,
      "end_seconds": 98.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.32,
      "end_seconds": 111.58,
      "duration_seconds": 11.26,
      "text": "I take Eno, when I get it. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.16,
      "end_seconds": 115.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Right. Okay, is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.38,
      "end_seconds": 119.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.54,
      "end_seconds": 121.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Alright, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.3,
      "end_seconds": 124.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "No, never had any surgery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.51,
      "end_seconds": 127.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.71,
      "end_seconds": 142.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.36,
      "end_seconds": 173.99,
      "duration_seconds": 12.63,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 76, BMI works out to 26.8. And height 165 centimetres, temperature 36.9, respiratory rate 15, weight 73 kilos, pressure 109 over 78. Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.0,
      "end_seconds": 181.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.24,
      "end_seconds": 184.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.72,
      "end_seconds": 186.42,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.65,
      "end_seconds": 190.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Turn your head to the side for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.93,
      "end_seconds": 200.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Tummy is soft and non-tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.64,
      "end_seconds": 210.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.66,
      "end_seconds": 212.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.08,
      "end_seconds": 224.47,
      "duration_seconds": 10.39,
      "text": "Putting it all together, I think we're dealing with gastro-oesophageal reflux at this stage. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.91,
      "end_seconds": 228.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.84,
      "end_seconds": 241.75,
      "duration_seconds": 12.91,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like gastro-oesophageal reflux, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had heartburn for two days, and no trouble swallowing or vomiting blood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.17,
      "end_seconds": 244.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.89,
      "end_seconds": 272.59,
      "duration_seconds": 27.7,
      "text": "Let's get an upper endoscopy, for persistent reflux. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. I'll start you on esomeprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast, for eight weeks. That should help with reflux. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Smaller dinners, earlier in the evening, and prop up the head of the bed with a couple of extra pillows."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.57,
      "end_seconds": 278.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.19,
      "end_seconds": 293.88,
      "duration_seconds": 14.69,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following. Please don't sit on it if the symptoms get worse. That's the point to get seen urgently. Come back in eight weeks. Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.43,
      "end_seconds": 303.05,
      "duration_seconds": 7.62,
      "text": "So, I take the esomeprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast and come back in eight weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.92,
      "end_seconds": 308.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. All right, I'll let you go. Any final questions first?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 310.35,
      "end_seconds": 313.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "That's all, thank you for your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.46,
      "end_seconds": 315.16,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}